-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulations 35 to 57: THE NOUNS shared by more than one
-- er3 module. Written by the piece agent er3 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30
-- (SOR-96-332.txt); nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
-- Types, constructors and fields of this piece begin `er3`; its rules begin `reg N`.
-- Nothing but DECLAREs lives here: no rule, no assertion.

§ `The purposes for which earnings are determined (reg 35)`

-- Reg 35(2) says the earnings it describes are taken into account for three purposes: whether an
-- interruption of earnings under (the Regulations') section 14 has occurred; the amount to be deducted
-- from benefits payable under the Act's ss 19, 21(3), 22(5), 152.03(3), 152.04(4) and 152.18; and
-- ss 45 and 46 of the Act. Reg 35(4) is limited to reg 14(2) and (5) and (6) to reg 14, so a purpose that
-- is "reg 14" is split into "reg 14(2)" and "reg 14, other than (2)": four constructors.
-- src:554 | (2) Subject to the other provisions of this section, the earnings to be taken into account for the purpose of determining whether an interruption of earnings under section 14 has occurred and the amount to be deducted from benefits payable under section 19, subsection 21(3), 22(5), 152.03(3) or 152.04(4) or section 152.18 of the Act, and to be taken into account for the purposes of sections 45 and 46 of the Act, are the entire income of a claimant arising out of any employment, including
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(2), (4), (5), (6) (src:554)
DECLARE `er3 Purpose of the determination of earnings` IS ONE OF
    `er3 purpose: an interruption of earnings under subsection 14(2) of the Regulations`
    `er3 purpose: an interruption of earnings under section 14 of the Regulations, other than subsection (2)`
    `er3 purpose: the amount to be deducted from benefits`
    `er3 purpose: sections 45 and 46 of the Act`

§ `The kinds of claimant for the value of income (reg 35(10))`

-- src:594 | (a) in the case of a claimant who is not self-employed, that amount of the claimant's income remaining after deducting
-- src:595 | (i) expenses incurred by the claimant for the direct purpose of earning that income, and
-- src:596 | (ii) the value of any consideration supplied by the claimant; and
-- src:597 | (b) in the case of a claimant who is self-employed in farming, the gross income from that self-employment, including any farming subsidies the claimant receives under any federal or provincial program, remaining after deducting the operating expenses, other than capital expenditures, incurred in that self-employment;
-- src:598 | (c) in the case of a claimant who is self-employed in employment other than farming, the amount of the gross income from that employment remaining after deducting the operating expenses, other than capital expenditures, incurred therein; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(10)(a)-(c) (src:594-598)
DECLARE `er3 Kind of claimant for the value of income` IS ONE OF
    `er3 claimant who is not self-employed`                                       -- (a)
    `er3 claimant who is self-employed in farming`                                -- (b)
    `er3 claimant who is self-employed in employment other than farming`         -- (c)

§ `Relationship to the claimant (regs 51.1(b), 55 and 55.01)`

-- Regs 55(1)(b), 55(2) and 55.01(1)(b), 55.01(2) use the same two lists, once with "claimant" and once with
-- "self-employed person" in the place of the person; one enum serves both, and `er3 someone else` is the
-- residue neither list reaches. "spouse or common-law partner" is one limb in the text, so it is one
-- constructor. Paragraph (h) of subsection (2) has two limbs and so two constructors.
-- src:817 | (b) for a period of not more than seven consecutive days to attend the funeral of a member of the claimant’s immediate family or of one of the following persons, namely,
-- src:818 | (i) a grandparent of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:819 | (ii) a grandchild of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:820 | (iii) the spouse or common-law partner of the claimant’s son or daughter or of the son or daughter of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:821 | (iv) the spouse or common-law partner of a child of the claimant’s father or mother or of a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the claimant’s father or mother,
-- src:822 | (v) a child of the father or mother of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the father or mother of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:823 | (vi) an uncle or aunt of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner, and
-- src:824 | (vii) a nephew or niece of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:831 | (a) the father and mother of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:832 | (b) the spouse or common-law partner of the father or mother of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:833 | (c) the foster parent of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:834 | (d) a child of the claimant’s father or mother or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the claimant’s father or mother;
-- src:835 | (e) the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:836 | (f) a child of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:837 | (g) a ward of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner; and
-- src:838 | (h) a dependant or relative residing in the claimant’s household or a relative with whom the claimant permanently resides.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(1)(b)(i)-(vii), 55(2)(a)-(h), 55.01(1)(b), 55.01(2) (src:817-824) (src:831-838)
DECLARE `er3 Relationship of a person to the claimant` IS ONE OF
    -- immediate family, reg 55(2)(a) to (h)
    `er3 a father or mother of the claimant or of the claimant's spouse or common-law partner`                         -- (a)
    `er3 the spouse or common-law partner of a father or mother of the claimant or of the claimant's spouse or common-law partner` -- (b)
    `er3 a foster parent of the claimant or of the claimant's spouse or common-law partner`                            -- (c)
    `er3 a child of the claimant's father or mother, or of the spouse or common-law partner of the claimant's father or mother` -- (d)
    `er3 the claimant's spouse or common-law partner`                                                                  -- (e)
    `er3 a child of the claimant or of the claimant's spouse or common-law partner`                                    -- (f)
    `er3 a ward of the claimant or of the claimant's spouse or common-law partner`                                     -- (g)
    `er3 a dependant or relative residing in the claimant's household`                                                 -- (h), first limb
    `er3 a relative with whom the claimant permanently resides`                                                        -- (h), second limb
    -- the further persons whose funeral the claimant may attend, reg 55(1)(b)(i) to (vii)
    `er3 a grandparent of the claimant or of the claimant's spouse or common-law partner`                              -- (i)
    `er3 a grandchild of the claimant or of the claimant's spouse or common-law partner`                               -- (ii)
    `er3 the spouse or common-law partner of the claimant's son or daughter, or of the son or daughter of the claimant's spouse or common-law partner` -- (iii)
    `er3 the spouse or common-law partner of a child of the claimant's father or mother, or of a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the claimant's father or mother` -- (iv)
    `er3 a child of the father or mother of the claimant's spouse or common-law partner, or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of that father or mother` -- (v)
    `er3 an uncle or aunt of the claimant or of the claimant's spouse or common-law partner`                           -- (vi)
    `er3 a nephew or niece of the claimant or of the claimant's spouse or common-law partner`                          -- (vii)
    -- anyone else
    `er3 someone else`
